<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 22 August, from 1138 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1138 <span class="tih-ago">888 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English forces defeat David I of Scotland at the Battle of the Standard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Northern English levies rallied round a cart bearing a ship's mast and sacred banners near Northallerton and routed King David I's army. It was a key battle of the civil war period known as the Anarchy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1485 <span class="tih-ago">541 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Tudor defeats and kills Richard III at Bosworth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard III was killed fighting at Bosworth Field when Lord Stanley's forces turned against him. Henry Tudor took the crown as Henry VII, founding the Tudor dynasty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1864 <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first Geneva Convention is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Twelve states signed the Geneva Convention protecting wounded soldiers and the medical staff caring for them. It grew out of Henry Dunant's campaign and founded modern humanitarian law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1902 <span class="tih-ago">124 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Cadillac Automobile Company is founded in Detroit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Investors reorganised Henry Ford's former company as Cadillac, named after the founder of Detroit. Engineer Henry Leland's precision manufacturing made it a byword for quality.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Walker flies the X-15 to the edge of space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA pilot Joseph Walker took the X-15 rocket plane to 107.8 km, beyond the 100 km boundary of space. The record for a winged aircraft stood until SpaceShipOne in 2004.</p></div></li></ol>
